  "question": {
    "text": "The random variable \\(\\mathrm{X}\\) has the following probability distribution\n\\(\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|}\n\\hline \\mathrm{x} & 0 & 1 & 2 & 3 & 4 \\\\\n\\hline \\mathrm{P}(\\mathrm{X}=\\mathrm{x}) & \\mathrm{k} & 3 \\mathrm{k} & 5 \\mathrm{k} & 2 \\mathrm{k} & \\mathrm{k} \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\\)\nThen the value of \\(P(X \\geq 2)\\) is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\)",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\\(\\frac{2}{3}\\)",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\\(\\frac{3}{4}\\)",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\\(\\frac{1}{4}\\)",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Since, \\(\\Sigma \\mathrm{P}_{\\mathrm{i}}(\\mathrm{X}=\\mathrm{x})=1\\)\n\\(\\begin{aligned}\n& \\therefore \\mathrm{k}+3 \\mathrm{k}+5 \\mathrm{k}+2 \\mathrm{k}+\\mathrm{k}=1 \\therefore 12 \\mathrm{k}=1 \\therefore \\mathrm{k}=\\frac{1}{12} \\\\\n& \\text { Now, } \\mathrm{P}(\\mathrm{X} \\geq 2)=\\mathrm{P}(\\mathrm{X}=2)+\\mathrm{P}(\\mathrm{X}=3)+\\mathrm{P}(\\mathrm{X}=4) \\\\\n& =5 \\mathrm{k}+2 \\mathrm{k}+\\mathrm{k}=8 \\mathrm{k}=8\\left(\\frac{1}{12}\\right)=\\frac{2}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\\)"
  }
}